Huffman Coding Implementation

DESCRIPTION:
This project implements the Huffman Encoding Algorithm as described in class.
The implementation is divided into three parts:

1. Huffman Encoder (encoder)
   - Takes text as input
   - Creates Huffman frequency map and tree
   - Encodes the text
   - Writes compressed file
   - Prints: input set, frequency map, tree structure

2. Huffman Decoder (decoder)
   - Takes compressed file as input
   - Reconstructs the original document
   - Writes reconstructed file
   - Prints: input set (compressed file info)

FILES:
1. Part 1.py   - Huffman encoding algorithm
2. Part 2.py   - Huffman decoding algorithm
3. README.txt          - This file

TEST TEXT USED:
The following text is used for testing (as provided in the assignment):

Hello World! This is a test of Huffman coding.
1234567890
Special characters: !@#$%^&*()_+-=[]{}|;:,.<>?
Multiple
lines
with
different
lengths.

HOW TO RUN:
Run Part 1 and then Run Part 2.

ALGORITHM DETAILS:
ENCODING ALGORITHM (encoder):
1. Read input text
2. Build frequency map (character -> count)
3. Build Huffman tree using priority queue
4. Generate Huffman codes from tree
5. Encode text using generated codes
6. Save to file with:
   - Frequency map (for reconstruction)
   - Padding information
   - Encoded bits

DECODING ALGORITHM (decoder):
1. Read compressed file
2. Extract frequency map
3. Rebuild Huffman tree (same as encoder)
4. Read encoded bits
5. Remove padding
6. Decode using Huffman tree
7. Save reconstructed text

FILE FORMAT (compressed.bin):
[Frequency map in format: "ASCII:count,ASCII:count,..."]
[Newline separator]
[8-bit padding information]
[Encoded bits (padded to multiple of 8)]

EXAMPLE OUTPUT:
When running Part 1 and Part 2, you will see:
1. ENCODER OUTPUT:
   - Input text (provided test content)
   - Frequency map (each character with count)
   - Huffman tree structure
   - File creation message

2. DECODER OUTPUT:
   - Compressed file information
   - Reconstruction status
   - File creation message